      "what": "an orc family hut: one round hut on a low wall of red terracotta over a blackstone footing, a domed roof of stretched hide on curved dark timber ribs, two great curved tusk timbers crossing over the door, iron spikes and a bone skull on the crown, a low broad door under a hide flap, a fire brazier and a weapon rack outside; two beds and a hearth inside",
      "form": "One round hut on a 12 x 12 plot (3 x 3 tiles of 4 blocks): about 10 across at the foot, a low wall 3 high, a stepped hide dome to a crown about 9 up. The roof is NOT a box: a low stone and terracotta wall (the skirt, 2-3 blocks) and then hide leaning in on curved timber ribs, stepping in every one or two blocks, so the outline is a curve from the wall top to the crown; the ribs stand proud and the great curved timbers (tusks) and iron spikes jut from the crown and the door.",
